From b7d49f39d53be586ae8d118fcd6b45ecccc032e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Velle Sinclair <brncomputerhelp@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 10:54:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 18/28] feat(web): implement Wallpaper Engine's web wallpaper
 API

Web wallpapers are written against an API the engine provides and none
of it existed: pages that call wallpaperRegisterAudioListener at load
threw and aborted their setup, and pages that build themselves in
wallpaperPropertyListener.applyUserProperties were never called. Ten of
the eleven web wallpapers in the test corpus rendered black.

- Install the API into the main frame's V8 context before the page's
  scripts run (OnContextCreated in the render process): the property
  listener (replayed for a listener assigned after delivery), the audio
  listener, wallpaperRequestRandomFileForProperty, and the media
  listeners, which report media integration as unavailable.
- After the main frame loads, deliver applyGeneralProperties ({fps}) and
  applyUserProperties from project.json, typed as project.json types
  them, with --set-property overrides applied, the defaults Wallpaper
  Engine gives unset values, and file and directory values made
  absolute. The delivery runs as a global-scope script so a listener
  declared with let or const is found.
- Feed audio listeners the 64-band spectrum for both channels each frame
  when the project supports audio processing.
- Log the page's console warnings and errors; they are the only account
  of why a web wallpaper drew nothing.

The payload is built by WebProperties, which has no CEF dependency and
is covered by unit tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tp4kQtVREMqxYupDoiqth6
